course: dictionary
lesson: 8971
title: Singular and plural
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Singular means one, and plural means more than one. «One cat sat on the mat» uses the singular cat. «Two cats sat on the mat» uses the plural cats. Look at the words around a word to see which form fits.
explain: Verbs must match the subject. «He runs to school» is singular, because he is one person. «They run to school» is plural, because they are more than one. When you read, check that the verb agrees with its noun.
explain: Some words are the same in both forms. «One sheep grazed in the field» and «Three sheep grazed in the field» both use sheep. Trust the context to tell you whether there is one or more.
fact: Singular means one thing; plural means more than one.
fact: The singular is the form of a noun for just one thing: «book» is the singular of «books».
fact: «Singular» can also mean very unusual or special, one of a kind. «A singular man» means a very strange or remarkable man.
fact: Some words are the same in singular and plural, like «one deer» and «two deer», or «one fish» and «three fish».
fact: Words like «trousers» and «scissors» are always plural, because they have two parts.
exercise: In «One cat sleeps by the fire», what form is cat? | Both singular and plural | *Singular, because there is one cat | Neither, because it is a verb | Plural, because it ends in s
exercise: «He ___ to school each day.» Which word fits? | running | ran | run | *runs
exercise: Find the one singular noun in «The children walked home while the boy waited.» | walked | children | *boy | waited
test: Which word is plural? | cat | bird | *books | book
test: In «one sheep, three sheep», what is true of sheep? | *The same in both forms | It changes to sheeps | Plural only | Singular only
exam: In «a singular man in a silver coat», what does singular suggest? | Tired and sleepy | *Very strange or remarkable | Plural, meaning more than one | Very quiet
